WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome to the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:04.000
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.901
-Thank you for having me.
-It is nice to see you.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.934
I'm a big fan of yours.
-I'm a big fan.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:10.567
-Wow. I love this.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.133
But how long are you
in New York for?

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:13.901
-I'm only here until tonight.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.601
I leave right after tonight.
-Okay.

00:00:15.601 --> 00:00:17.467
-Right after this.
-Have you had fun?

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.200
-Say hi to my Philly people,
the Roots. Hey y'all.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.634
-Yep, yep.
-I've had a good time.

00:00:22.634 --> 00:00:24.901
I had to come do
a Disney event yesterday.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:26.501
-Yeah.
-Or Monday.

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:29.334
I had to do a Disney event
where you go, like, tell people

00:00:29.334 --> 00:00:31.534
what your show's about
and they give you money.

00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:32.868
Um, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:35.267
And that was fine?
It all went well?

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:38.767
-Except for I ran
into the ever-elusive,

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:42.033
ever-terrifying David Blaine.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:43.801
I almost said David Spade
because I just saw him,

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:45.300
but he's wonderful.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.834
No. David Blaine
did magic to me.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.167
He did magic to me, y'all!

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:50.367
-Wait. What do you mean?

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:51.801
What do you mean
he did magic to you?

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.300
-To me.
-No, no. What do you mean?

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:56.100
-I mean, he walked up
to a group of people.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.300
David Blaine has an exciting
new show coming out,

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.234
so free promo for him, but...

00:01:01.234 --> 00:01:03.968
He was testing the magic out,
and he came up to me

00:01:03.968 --> 00:01:06.133
and I was talking
to a man from ESPN.

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:08.767
And he asked, "You guys
want to see a magic trick?"

00:01:08.767 --> 00:01:12.167
My Christian Black self
said, "No."

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:14.234
Very quickly.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.868
But the man I was with said,
"Yes," and he heard that "yes."

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.634
That man had a big, deep voice.
He went, "Yes."

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:20.567
So it was like --
That's what he heard.

00:01:20.567 --> 00:01:22.234
-Yeah.
-So he takes out the card.

00:01:22.234 --> 00:01:23.701
He has me put my hand in a fist.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.834
I'm scared of him.
I just want y'all to know.

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:27.234
That's why I didn't do anything.

00:01:27.234 --> 00:01:28.601
-He's been on the show.
Yeah, he's --

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:30.634
-He's scary. I heard he
coughed up frogs or something?

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:32.400
-He threw up a frog, yeah,
on our show, yeah.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.734
-That's scary. It's funny and --
But it's scary, so...

00:01:34.734 --> 00:01:36.534
-Yeah, Questlove
passed out, yeah.

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.100
-Did he?
-Yeah, he passed out.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.367
Wait. So he --

00:01:39.367 --> 00:01:40.634
-Okay, so he tells me
to put my hand in a fist.

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:42.634
-Uh-huh.
-So I put my hand in a fist.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:45.534
But the other hand --
He says, "Here, pick a card."

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:48.234
I pick a card. He said pick --
You know, whatever.

00:01:48.234 --> 00:01:50.300
"What's the card?"
I say, "8 of diamonds."

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:51.634
And he said, "Oh, okay.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:53.734
Well, then pick
either 8 or diamonds."

00:01:53.734 --> 00:01:56.267
And so I picked an 8,
and he was like,

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.501
"Open your other hand."

00:01:57.501 --> 00:02:00.334
There was an "8"
written on my hand.

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:03.133
-No, he's amazing. So that's it.
That's when you leave, right?

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:04.767
-I almost closed
the fist back up

00:02:04.767 --> 00:02:06.367
and punched him in the face!

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:08.067
-You go, "I'm getting out."

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:09.501
-That's when you think
it's over.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:11.300
I said, "Okay, thank you, David.
Thank you."

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:13.267
And I was secretly like...

00:02:13.267 --> 00:02:16.234
So, then I tweeted about it,

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:18.701
because I wanted people
to pray for me after that.

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:20.934
So I tweeted -- I did.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:22.501
I don't mess with magic, y'all.

00:02:22.501 --> 00:02:24.834
I wasn't allowed to watch
"Harry Potter."

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:28.033
I don't even watch the team
the Magic play.

00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:29.334
I don't --
-You did tweet it.

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:30.601
-[ Laughter ]
-I don't!

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:32.567
I'm not watching it.
-Orlando Magic, no.

00:02:32.567 --> 00:02:35.234
You go, "David Blaine
just did magic to me.

00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:38.200
This is not a joke.
Please pray for me for real.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:40.734
Just rolled up on me and
magic'ed all over the place."

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:42.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.501 --> 00:02:44.367
[ Applause ]

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.734
-I wanted prayer and protection.
-Yes.

00:02:50.734 --> 00:02:55.000
-I wanted -- So, I tweet that.
I think everything's fine.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.901
-Yeah.
-I have wine.

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:58.567
I have a good time.
-Sure.

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:01.200
-Later on in the night, David
Blaine does his presentation,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.367
because he has his new show
on Nat Geo.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:04.968
And at the end of it, he's like,

00:03:04.968 --> 00:03:07.367
"And my next guest actually
tweeted about me tonight."

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:09.534
And I was like, "No!"

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:11.400
-"We're done! We're done, man!
We're good!"

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.067
-And I was like,
"I'm not getting up."

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:15.334
And he's like, "That's okay.
I'll come over to you."

00:03:15.334 --> 00:03:17.100
That's not his voice.
I'm making him way more --

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:18.400
I don't know
what he sounds like.

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.901
-Yeah, he doesn't talk
like that at all.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.234
-He doesn't talk like that
at all.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:23.300
-"I'm coming over to you!"
That's not David Blaine.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.033
He's very like --
-Yeah, he's actually...

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:27.267
-"I'll come over to you."
-Yeah, that is what he's like.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:28.734
That's really good.
-Yeah, thank you.

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:30.367
-So he goes,
"I'll come over to you!"

00:03:30.367 --> 00:03:32.133
And then...
-David Blaine.

00:03:32.133 --> 00:03:34.167
-Comes over,
and he sits next to me,

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:36.701
and then he says,
"Is this your wine?

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.300
Can I have a sip?"

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.133
In my head,
I'm saying, "No. COVID."

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:43.467
But then I couldn't say anything
because I was so scared.

00:03:43.467 --> 00:03:45.000
And I said, "Please don't
make me disappear."

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.567
And he said,
"I just want to know

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.200
if I can have
a sip of your wine."

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:50.734
And I didn't say anything,
and he bit my wine glass

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:52.300
and chewed it and ate it.

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.934
[ Audience groans ]

00:03:53.934 --> 00:03:56.934
-He ate the glass?
-He ate the glass.

00:03:58.367 --> 00:04:01.267
-He ate the glass and ate it.

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:02.767
The guy is unbelievable.

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:05.300
-You see this?
That's not even the worst part.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:07.100
-Yes, it is.
-No, it's not.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:09.767
So then I'm sitting there
minding my business.

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.033
This is happening to me.

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:13.534
And then he says, "Pick a card."

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.534
I said, "I did that once,
and look where we are."

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:18.801
So I had to do it,
and then I picked a card.

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:20.868
And then it was 8
of something else.

00:04:20.868 --> 00:04:22.000
I think 8 of clubs.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.834
And he said,
"Here, put it in my wallet."

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:25.334
I said, "Okay.
Please get away from me."

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.300
And then he did a move
and he was like,

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.534
"I'm going make it change
into the 8 of hearts."

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:31.434
I was like, "Whatever."
So I just opened the wallet.

00:04:31.434 --> 00:04:33.167
It's not there.
I said, "The card's not there.

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.200
You suck. No."

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.734
But then --

00:04:36.734 --> 00:04:38.200
-It's unbelievable, this story.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.968
-Isn't it ridic--
I promise it's ending soon.

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:41.434
-No, I love it.

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:43.701
-Oh, before that, he took
a picture of the card

00:04:43.701 --> 00:04:45.067
in my phone, you guys.

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.834
My phone,
Quinta Brunson's phone.

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:49.334
Took a picture,
and it was the 8 of clubs,

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:50.968
and he put my phone down.

00:04:50.968 --> 00:04:52.467
Opens his wallet.
The card's not there.

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:54.734
He says --
I said, "Oh, you messed up."

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:57.400
He said, "No, I didn't.
Look at your phone."

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.033 --> 00:05:00.567
-Again, if you close your eyes,

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:01.834
it's like David Blaine
is right here.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.167
"Look at your phone!"

00:05:03.167 --> 00:05:04.868
-I look at the picture
in my phone.

00:05:04.868 --> 00:05:06.534
It had changed
to the 8 of hearts.

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:08.501
And that's when I was like,
you know what?

00:05:08.501 --> 00:05:10.467
No -- I don't mess with him.

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:12.868
So, David, if you're watching
this, don't play with me.

00:05:12.868 --> 00:05:14.267
Don't -- Don't --

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:16.934
I'm not playing with you
because --

00:05:16.934 --> 00:05:20.567
-Alright. We get it.
David, we love you.

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:22.701
Quinta, I want to talk
about "Abbott Elementary."

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:24.367
-Yes, yes.
-Congrats on the show.

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:25.868
-Thank you.
-I heard about it.

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:27.200
Everyone loves it. I go --

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:30.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Thank you, guys.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.367
-Do you know, the show's
audience has quadrupled

00:05:33.367 --> 00:05:34.968
since the pilot first aired.

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:36.901
Quadrupled.
-Quadrupled.

00:05:36.901 --> 00:05:38.701
-Yeah, that is --
It's a massive hit.

00:05:38.701 --> 00:05:40.734
And I heard about this,
and someone's like,

00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:42.033
"Trust me.
You got to watch this."

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:45.300
And I go, "I'll check it out."
It is so funny.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:47.100
It's just -- I haven't seen

00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:50.501
a really kind of funny
new sitcom in years.

00:05:50.501 --> 00:05:51.601
-Thank you!

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:53.601
-And it's kind of
like mockumentary style

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:55.667
set in an elementary school.

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:57.567
And it's funny. And I mean --

00:05:57.567 --> 00:05:59.868
How do you set it up for people
if you haven't seen it?

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:01.400
It's for the family, by the way.
Everyone.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:03.767
-Yes.
To set it up, it is a show

00:06:03.767 --> 00:06:05.934
about a group of schoolteachers
in Philadelphia.

00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:07.501
It was inspired by my mom,

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.200
who was a kindergarten teacher
in Philadelphia.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:10.634
She was my kindergarten teacher.

00:06:10.634 --> 00:06:12.100
And then I went to the school

00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:14.100
where she taught
for the next five years,

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.367
and so I just got to see
a lot of behind the scenes,

00:06:16.367 --> 00:06:18.300
which kind of inspired
the mockumentary style,

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:19.767
just being behind the scenes.

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:21.667
And it's about teachers
who do their very best

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:25.100
in a Philadelphia public school,
which is very funny, and...

00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:26.601
-That's right.

00:06:26.601 --> 00:06:29.601
--...inspiring and interesting
and makes you think a little bit

00:06:29.601 --> 00:06:31.501
about the state
of public schools in America.

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:34.234
-That's right. I love it.
It's a great show.

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:36.234
You do a great job.
-You're so funny.

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:38.067
The writers. Great job.
-They're so great.

00:06:38.067 --> 00:06:39.667
-Everybody. Actors.
Everyone's good.

00:06:39.667 --> 00:06:40.968
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:40.968 --> 00:06:42.767
Here's Quinta Brunson
in "Abbott Elementary."

00:06:42.767 --> 00:06:44.000
Take a look.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:46.033
-So this Zach,
he lives with you?

00:06:46.033 --> 00:06:47.734
-Yeah, he just moved in
last month.

00:06:47.734 --> 00:06:51.033
-And that's going well?
-Yep, he's so great.

00:06:51.033 --> 00:06:55.767
-So, he knew you
and was like, "More!"

00:06:55.767 --> 00:06:57.801
-Well, I think he sounds like
a really neat guy, right?

00:06:57.801 --> 00:07:00.601
-Oh, sure. Oh, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:07:00.601 --> 00:07:02.767
-Hey, there's my guy.
-Black?

00:07:02.767 --> 00:07:06.434
-It's actually pronounced Zach.
You must be Ava.

00:07:06.434 --> 00:07:07.734
-You were all thinking it.

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:09.267
I see you.
Don't look at me like that.

00:07:09.267 --> 00:07:10.634
-We always look at you
like this.

00:07:10.634 --> 00:07:12.767
-It's very nice
to meet you, Zach.

00:07:12.767 --> 00:07:15.701
-Well, if it isn't
my pizza-crust queen.

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:19.234
-We went out to eat last week,
and I ate all his pizza crust.

00:07:19.234 --> 00:07:21.634
I don't like to waste food.

00:07:21.634 --> 00:07:25.133
-It's fast. It's funny.
Quinta Brunson.

00:07:25.133 --> 00:07:27.467
Check out the first season
of "Abbott Elementary"

00:07:27.467 --> 00:07:30.200
streaming now on Hulu.
Come back whenever you want.

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:31.968
Thank you so much.
-I will. I will.

